OL,3,GNEWSAHeat raises costs and cuts crop
OL,4,Ayields for farmers
OL,5,
OL,6,FFarmers in Jersey say the hot weather
OL,7,Fhas caused a number of problems this
OL,8,Fyear, including significant reductions
OL,9,Fto their harvests and mounting watering
OL,10,Fcosts.
OL,12,FAt the beginning of September, Jersey
OL,13,FMet Office confirmed this summer was
OL,14,Fthe warmest since records began in
OL,15,F1894.
OL,17,FChristine Hellio, from Manor Farm, said
OL,18,Fshe had "never had to irrigate pumpkins
OL,19,Fto this extreme before". Meanwhile
OL,20,Fproducers of apples and cereals said
OL,21,Ftheir harvests were down 90% and 50%
OL,22,Frespectively.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
